Article 65

1. In the framework of effective implementation of CFC policy in the Region, a CFC Task Force is formed.
2. Formation and membership composition of the CFC Task Force is stipulated by Regent's Decree.
3. Regent appoints the head of Bappeda as CFC Task Force and the head of OPD in charge of women's empowerment as secretary of the CFC Task Force;
4. CFC Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), has the main duties of:a. coordinating the implementation of CFC policy and development; b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on CFC policy;
c. collecting basic data for CFC development;
d. conducting needs analysis sourced from basic data; e. conducting dissemination of basic data;
f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing CFC, which are adjusted to regional potential;
g. preparing a 5 (five) year Child-Friendly City regional action plan and work mechanism; andh. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least 1 (one) time per year.
